{"name":"Northampton Trees","hex":"#767962","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trees","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tree"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of tree"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trees"}],"entries":[{"title":"Northampton","blocks":[{"text":"Northampton is a town and civil parish in Northamptonshire, England. It is the county town of Northamptonshire and the administrative centre of the unitary authority of West Northamptonshire. The town is situated on the River Nene, 60 miles (97 km) north-west of London and 50 miles (80 km) south-east of Birmingham. Northampton is one of the largest towns in England; the population of its overall urban area was recorded as 249,093 in the 2021 census. The parish of Northampton alone had 137,387."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Northampton_Guildhall_01.jpg/330px-Northampton_Guildhall_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northampton","wikidata":"Q192240"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Northampton_lift_tower_8.06.jpg/500px-Northampton_lift_tow